                <note rend="inline" type="source">365D.1163/73: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-05-05T15:00:00+01:00">May 5, 1937—3 p.m.</date><lb/>[Received
                        May 5—11:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>200. Embassy’s 159, April 14, 7 p.m. Foreign Office informs me that Ministry of
                    Colonies has ascertained that the report of the expulsion of the three members
                    of the American Bible Missionary Society, referred to in paragraph 2 of the
                    Embassy’s telegram 152 of April 9, 6 p.m., is unfounded and that the
                    missionaries in question are still in Addis Ababa.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
